  <static seed="1998" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/Percent/MTH20PercentApplicationType3_20.pg">
    <statement><p>In the last election, <m>49\%</m> of a county<rsq/>s residents, or <m>9359</m> people, turned out to vote. How many residents live in this county?</p>
<p>This county has <fillin characters="9" name="AnSwEr0001"/> residents.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>19100</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This problem can be boiled down to this question: <m>9359</m> is <m>49\%</m> of what? We will show multiple methods to solve this problem.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 1</p>
<p>We will use proportion to solve this problem. Assume <m>9359</m> is <m>49\%</m> of <m>x</m>, so <lq/><m>49</m> out of <m>100</m><rq/> corresponds to <lq/><m>9359</m> out of <m>x</m><rq/>.</p>
<p>We will write and solve the proportion:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \frac{49}{100} \amp = \frac{9359}{x} \\
   49x \amp = 100 \cdot 9359 \\
   49x \amp = 935900 \\
   \frac{49x}{49} \amp = \frac{935900}{49} \\
   x \amp = 19100
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>This county has <m>19100</m> residents.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 2</p>
<p>We will use the percentage formula to solve this problem. This translation from English to math may help you remember the percentage formula.</p>
<p><m>2 \text{ is } 50\% \text{ of } 4 \iff 2 = 0.5 \cdot 4</m></p>
<p>The question is: <m>9359</m> is <m>49\%</m> of what? Assume <m>9359</m> is <m>49\%</m> of <m>x</m>. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}
        9359  \amp  = 0.49 \cdot x \\
        \frac{9359}{0.49} \amp  = \frac{0.49x}{0.49} \\
        19100 \amp = x
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>This county has <m>19100</m> residents.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 3</p>
<p>In the sentence <lq/><m>9359</m> is <m>49\%</m> of what,<rq/></p>
<p><ul label="disc">
<li>
<p><m>9359</m> is the <alert>percentage</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>49\%</m> is the <alert>rate</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><lq/>what<rq/> is the <alert>base</alert> (following the word <lq/>of<rq/>).</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>By the formula <m>\text{base} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{rate}}</m>, we do a division to solve the problem:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{base} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{rate}} = \frac{9359}{49\%} = \frac{9359}{0.49} = 19100 }</m></p>
<p>This county has <m>19100</m> residents.</p>
</solution>
